{"full":"hf:imageomics/Andromeda","spaceId":"imageomics/Andromeda","name":"Andromeda","source":"huggingface","description":"Interactive tool for visualizing high-dimensional data using weighted multidimensional scaling.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","data-visualization","data-analysis","exploration","data","visualization","clustering","EDA","dimensionality-reduction","MDS","data-exploration","visual-analytics","human-in-the-loop","weighted-multi-dimensional-scaling","interactive-evaluation","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":4,"created":"2023-08-11T17:05:19.000Z","updated":"2025-12-15T15:44:06.000Z","license":"mit","runtime":"SLEEPING","appUrl":"https://imageomics-andromeda.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/imageomics/Andromeda","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:32:04.671Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:32:04.671Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:32:04.671Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"👀","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Andromeda allows users to visualize high dimensional data in a 2-dimensional plot using weighted multidimensional scaling. Through the interactive interface users can explore the relationships within their data by adjusting the variable weights and viewing an updated plot. Alternatively users can arrange the items in the plot so that Andromeda can determine new variable weights and create a new projection.","The Fetch image data tab gives users the ability to fetch data from iNaturalist observations and pair them with satellite RGB and landcover data for analysis with Andromeda.","This Andromeda instance allows users to perform dimensional reduction on an uploaded CSV file. A toy sample CSV for trying the interface can be found on the GitHub Repository."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/imageomics/Andromeda/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a9515a76f80b2c98a88ca7c5bfb2ddcae6c042f265b8f0a67d07fc2a7d994